{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/strict"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy\/strict"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials8CalendarV14MatchingPolicyO6strictyA2EmF","title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.strict","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"strict","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"case"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Working with matching policies","anchor":"Working-with-matching-policies","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/nextTime","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/nextTimePreservingSmallerComponents","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/previousTimePreservingSmallerComponents"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"strict"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, if searching for Feb 29 in the Gregorian calendar, the algorithm may choose March 1 instead (for example, if the year is not a leap year). If you wish to find the next Feb 29 without the algorithm adjusting the next higher component in the specified "},{"code":"DateComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then use the "},{"code":"strict","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There are ultimately implementation-defined limits in how far distant the search will go.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"If specified, the algorithm travels as far forward or backward as necessary looking for a match.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar/MatchingPolicy/strict":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy\/strict","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"strict","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/strict","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If specified, the algorithm travels as far forward or backward as necessary looking for a match."}],"title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.strict"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar/MatchingPolicy/nextTime":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy\/nexttime","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nextTime","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/nextTime","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If there is no matching time before the end of the next instance of the next higher component to the highest specified component in the "},{"code":"DateComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" argument, the algorithm will return the next existing time which exists."}],"title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.nextTime"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Calendar","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Calendar","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A definition of the relationships between calendar units and absolute points in time, providing features for calculation and comparison of dates."}],"title":"Calendar"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials":{"title":"FoundationEssentials","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Access essential data types, collections, and operating-system services to define the base layer of functionality for your app."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar/MatchingPolicy/previousTimePreservingSmallerComponents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/previousTimePreservingSmallerComponents","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy\/previoustimepreservingsmallercomponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If there is no matching time before the end of the next instance of the next higher component to the highest specified component in the "},{"code":"DateComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" argument, the algorithm will return the previous existing value of the missing component and preserves the lower components’ values."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.previousTimePreservingSmallerComponents","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"previousTimePreservingSmallerComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar/MatchingPolicy/nextTimePreservingSmallerComponents":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy\/nexttimepreservingsmallercomponents","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nextTimePreservingSmallerComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy\/nextTimePreservingSmallerComponents","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"If specified, and there is no matching time before the end of the next instance of the next higher component to the highest specified component in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DateComponents"},{"text":" argument, the method will return the next existing value of the missing component and preserves the lower components’ values (e.g., no 2:37am results in 3:37am, if that exists).","type":"text"}],"title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.nextTimePreservingSmallerComponents"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/Calendar/MatchingPolicy":{"title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MatchingPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Calendar\/MatchingPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calendar\/matchingpolicy","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A hint to the search algorithm to control the method used for searching for dates."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MatchingPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}